  <h2>About</h2>
  <p>I graduated with high honors from Tarrant County College this past May and am currently pursuing a Bachelor’s degree in Leadership Studies with a minor in Human Resources at Texas Tech University.

Alongside my studies, I bring more than 18 years of operational and customer experience leadership across healthcare, retail, finance, and travel, leading multi-tiered, multi-site teams of up to 350 people. My background includes serving as a Customer Experience Director and Site Manager—directing large-scale contact centers, high-volume processing operations, and workforce capacity models—as well as senior department management focused on quality assurance and operational execution.

Outside of work, I’m deeply invested in community and organizational leadership, including serving as the founding Chapter President of the Delta Chi Chapter of Tri Psi Sorority at Tulane University, a longtime Girl Scout leader and Service Unit Executive Board member, and a Project Graduation Co-Chair. Across every role, I’m driven by encouraging, motivating, and developing people to do their best work and create lasting impact.

#Leadership #HumanResources #CustomerExperience #OperationsLeadership #PeopleDevelopment
</p>
